-- title:
--   Rational places over a supersingular point: node or disc (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and a guard prime $\ell_g$ is fixed with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$.
--
--   **Supersingular place and constant reduction.** $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose membership is, by `hW`, equivalent to membership in `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: $w$ is rational, is an affine geometric place, and $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. It is assumed that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (hypothesis `hle`), where the first is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full modular function field of level $M'$ inside Laurent series and the second is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the $X_H$-function field at level $q^2M'$ for $H=\ker(\mathrm{ZMod}\,(q^2M')^\times\to \mathrm{ZMod}\,q^\times)$ (written `levelH q M'`). The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A,M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, agreement with $A$ on constants, the scaling condition that every nonzero $f$ admits $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue, and a place map preserving degrees and orders. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$.
--
--   **The descent field $k_0$ (group `hdvr`–`hκ`).** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ has $\pi_0\in A$; the valuation ring $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is assumed to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and $k_0$ is assumed to meet every residue class: every $a\in A$ differs from some $c\in k_0\cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary level data.** $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b=\bot$; $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$; and $\varpi_b\ne 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ obtained by composing $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and asserts the following for all data as below.
--
--   Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and $W_0$ a valuation subring of $F_0$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff its image in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; and the linear disjointness condition holds: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent, and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i \iota(c_i)\,a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   Let $B$ be a subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` subject to the following group of hypotheses: the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; $B$ is contained in the compositum $L:=\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of }K_b)\sqcup F_0$ and every element of $L$ is a fraction $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is the corresponding localisation, i.e. $f\in W_0$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ coming from $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,j_q$ lies in $B$; and $B$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta:\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   A further hypothesis identifies the special fibre of $B$ with a Drinfeld quotient: for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ for which $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ is a domain, and every $\zeta:\mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,C_s$ with: $\#C_s=\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ (for $q=2$ this width is $12$ or $1$ according as the $j$-value vanishes or not, divided by the $j$-ramification of $s$); $\ker\rho$ the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ on constants given by the residue map of $A$ followed by the structure map; every element of the quotient field a fraction $\rho g/\rho h$; the image of $\rho$ characterised by membership, in the Drinfeld function field, of the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}$; and equivariance: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)\in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $f\in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}f\in B$, the element $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}f)$ is the $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ of $\langle(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)\rangle$ applied to $\rho f$.
--
--   A rationality hypothesis (RAT) requires that every $f\in\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Let $\mathrm{nodes}$ be a finite set of subrings of $F_0$ satisfying the valuative **cover** hypothesis over $s$: for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which agrees with $A$ on $k_0$ and which lies over $s$ in the sense that for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, has non-negative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $j_q$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$, lies in $V$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ — for every such $V$, either every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or some $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ is dominated by $V$, meaning every $f\in O$ lies in $V$ and every non-unit of $O$ lands in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Let $FSS$ be a field with a $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-algebra structure and $R$ a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map onto $FSS$ with kernel the maximal ideal, agreement with $A$ on constants, and the scaling condition), such that for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ iff $f\in W_0$.
--
--   Finally, let $N$ be a finite set of places of $FSS$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, let $Q\mapsto S_Q$ assign subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, let $\varphi_Q:A_b[X]\to S_Q$ and $\chi_Q:S_Q\to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ be ring homomorphisms, and let $Q\mapsto D_Q$ assign sets of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, subject to the following conjunction of hypotheses on ends, base-smooth point stalks and residue discs. First, $\#N=q+1$. Second, $Q\notin N$ exactly when the $R$-residue of every element of $B$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ belongs to the valuation subring of $Q$. Third, for each $Q\notin N$ a list of clauses holds: the image of $A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for $a\in A_b$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q X)=0$; $S_Q$ is local with $\ker\chi_Q$ its maximal ideal; $S_Q\subseteq L$ and every element of $L$ is a fraction of elements of $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; all elements of $S_Q$ lie in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ iff it is divisible by $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$; for $f\in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_Q f$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q X$ has $Q$-order $1$; $B\subseteq S_Q$, and $f\in S_Q$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ such that the residue of the $R$-residue of $h$ at $Q$ is nonzero; and $P\in D_Q$ iff $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for every $f\in S_Q$ the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_Q f=0$. Fourth, the discs are pairwise disjoint: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, a common $P\in D_Q\cap D_{Q'}$ forces $Q=Q'$. Fifth, for $Q\notin N$ every $P\in D_Q$ has non-negative order at the image of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,j_q$. Sixth, equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta:\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residual automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ preserves $N$ as a set, and for $Q\notin N$ one has $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_Q)=D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is rational and which lies over $s$ in the following sense — for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ having non-negative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which the $j$-element has non-negative order and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$ — exactly one of two alternatives is asserted as a disjunction: either there is $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ with $O$ contained in the valuation subring of $P$ (every $f\in O$ lies in $P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$) and such that for every non-unit $f$ of $O$ the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$; or there is a place $Q\notin N$ with $P\in D_Q$.
--
--   This is the step, for $q=2$ at a rigid auxiliary level, which transfers the valuative cover of the descended supersingular model to individual rational places: a rational place of the geometric function field specialising to the supersingular point $s$ either dominates one of the finitely many node rings or lies in one of the residue discs attached to the base-smooth points of the chart $B$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd) in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at level divisible by $q^2$.
